BLE Wide was extracted from the working tree of w1700k-sdr on 2026-10-17.
Source: https://github.com/h0m3us3r/w1700k-sdr
Working branch: codex/ble-advertising-dsp
Base commit: 05adca1609ab806a88af0b1b4831df2ee41d6bb8
The extraction includes local development beyond that commit.

The MIT notice in LICENSE is retained for inherited source.
include/iq4.h, include/iq8.h and include/w1700k_stream.h are vendored
format/shared-memory interfaces from that working tree; no router checkout
is needed to build. airspace/advertisements.py derives from host/ble/server.py.
The test bit sequence is identified in tests/python/fixtures.py.

The receiver/ UDP ingest service and include/{fft.h,posix.h} and mk/platform.mk also
come from host/stream and host/common in that working tree.
include/uapi/w1700k_sdr.h retains GPL-2.0 WITH Linux-syscall-note; it is
a Linux userspace interface, not firmware. Its SPDX license applies to that file.

Router firmware, DSP research, per-device credentials,
recordings, compiler profiles and build outputs are not part of this repo.

receiver/usb/helper.mm uses the RTL8157 register/enable sequence from Linux
drivers/net/usb/r8152.c (Realtek and Linux contributors), commit 58161ead29e50d70a317ea26b472e0c7508e69da.
That separate executable is GPL-2.0-only; see LICENSES/GPL-2.0.
Other new USB transport/parser code carries its own MIT SPDX notice.

receiver/usb/rtl8157-init.h and rtl8157-data.h port initialization and
firmware/register tables from Realtek r8152 v2.22.1, Copyright (c) 2024
Realtek Semiconductor Corp. All rights reserved., under GPL-2.0-only.
Pinned source: https://github.com/awesometic/realtek-r8152-dkms/blob/d93c9f89ca5a831c9437e35319c546e48c710f9a/src/r8152.c
tools/usb/import-rtl8157.py reproduces the tables from that source and
verifies its SHA-256 before importing. These files are compiled into the
separate GPL-2.0-only helper; see LICENSES/GPL-2.0.
